Keep the arty200t TACIT configs on the branch predictor they were measured with.

patches/0030 flips chipyard.WithTacitEncoder's default to useBP = false, which is
right for this tutorial (the predictor is dead logic in BrTarget mode, and BrTarget
is the only mode the PYNQ-Z1 labs use) but is NOT this repo's decision to make for
the riskybird arty200t work that shares the donor Chipyard tree.

fpga/src/main/scala/arty200t/TacitAccelConfigs.scala is the one TRACKED file in
that tree that consumes the fragment. Making the `true` explicit there keeps
RocketArty200TDroneGemminiSaturnFp16At35TacitConfig elaborating exactly what it
elaborated before. Its sibling fragment WithTacitEncoderBP already constructs
TacitBPParams directly, and `enable` defaults to true, so nEntries = 256 / 128
configs are unaffected without touching them.

Unlike 0030, this file IS in git, so scripts/02_verify_patches.sh checks it.

diff --git a/fpga/src/main/scala/arty200t/TacitAccelConfigs.scala b/fpga/src/main/scala/arty200t/TacitAccelConfigs.scala
index 6fea2d8f..7ecb3d49 100644
--- a/fpga/src/main/scala/arty200t/TacitAccelConfigs.scala
+++ b/fpga/src/main/scala/arty200t/TacitAccelConfigs.scala
@@ -59,9 +59,12 @@ class WithTacitEncoderBP(nEntries: Int = 1024, bufferDepth: Int = 16) extends Co
 })
 
 // Full-strength TACIT (1024-entry BP): DMA sink (target id 1) + encoder.
+// useBP = true is explicit because chipyard.WithTacitEncoder now defaults the DSC
+// branch predictor OFF -- it is dead logic in BrTarget mode, which is the only mode
+// the PYNQ-Z1 tutorial uses. This config keeps the predictor, so it is unchanged.
 class WithTacitDmaTrace extends Config(
   new tacit.WithTraceSinkDMA(1) ++
-  new chipyard.WithTacitEncoder)
+  new chipyard.WithTacitEncoder(useBP = true))
 
